WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.978
Integers are whole numbers that can be positive or negative. Zero is in the middle.

00:07.428 --> 00:13.419
Positive numbers are to the right of zero. Negative numbers are to the left.

00:13.869 --> 00:21.362
Adding a positive number moves right. Start at negative two, add three, and hop right three times.

00:21.362 --> 00:23.273
You land on positive one.

00:23.723 --> 00:31.029
Adding a negative number moves left. Start at one, add negative four, and hop left four times.

00:31.029 --> 00:33.127
You land on negative three.

00:33.577 --> 00:41.240
A positive one and a negative one cancel each other out, and make zero. We call them a zero pair.
